    {
      "id": "short",
      "type": "inspect.fit_circle_arc",
      "name": "Reject insufficient angular support",
      "documentation": "<p>Circle fitting minimizes squared radial distances. A normalized algebraic initializer and SVD-based refinement are separate from minimum enclosing circles. RANSAC refits stable consensus support. Short or ill-conditioned arcs withhold the primary geometry; valid circle and ordered-arc states are reported separately.</p><p>Uncertainty is a conditional radial-IID linearization, not calibration or manufacturing uncertainty. Angular support is an envelope of observed directions, not visibility or occlusion evidence.</p><p><a href=\"https://arxiv.org/abs/cs/0301001\">Chernov and Lesort: Least squares fitting of circles and lines</a>. The block uses a bounded CPU implementation; it does not claim a native OpenCV fitCircle binding.</p>",
      "parameters": {
        "method": "ransac",
        "item_index": 0,
        "boundary_index": -1,
        "path": "auto",
        "inlier_tolerance": 1.0,
        "maximum_trials": 256,
        "confidence": 0.99,
        "random_seed": 0,
        "refinement_iterations": 50,
        "position_tolerance": 1e-08,
        "minimum_inliers": 6,
        "minimum_inlier_fraction": 0.5,
        "minimum_span_degrees": 30.0,
        "maximum_condition": 10000.0,
        "maximum_gap_degrees": 120.0,
        "maximum_backtracking_fraction": 0.1,
        "minimum_radius": 0.01,
        "maximum_radius": 10000000.0,
        "check_rmse": true,
        "maximum_rmse": 1.0,
        "sample_limit": 2000
      },
